  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Representing Victims of Trafficking for Access to Comprehensive Justice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In partnership with the NEXUS Institute and Instituto Tecnolgico Autnomo de Mxico (ITAM), the University of Michigan Law Schools Human Trafficking Clinic is now establishing a model legal clinic in Mexico City focused on building the capacity for legal advocacy and direct representation of VoTs in criminal and civil proceedings. The curriculum developed for clinic students will advocate a victim centered approach and assist in replicating the clinic throughout Mexico. Project was launched in Mexico City because of security and safety concerns in Zacatecas.</narrative>
  </description>
